// Change: new rule
// Title: Alternate Data Stream Manipulation Via Streams.EXE
// Sigma ID: 03d5e4aa-7040-464f-80bf-0744c3c20f19
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: EinLamYe
// Date: 2026-06-29 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1564.004, T1070
// Description: Detects execution of the Sysinternals Streams utility, used to enumerate or delete NTFS
//   Alternate Data Streams. Adversaries abuse it to inspect, strip Mark-of-the-Web, or remove ADS-
//   hidden payloads as an anti-forensic / defense-evasion action.
// False positives:
//   - Administrators inspecting alternate data streams
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sysinternals/downloads/streams
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/c5875f6ddd2f5087d0f0a63a34a2ed4468a9d328/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_streams_ads_manipulation.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\streams.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\streams64.exe") or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "streams.exe"
